12979	{"artifactId":"LLD-0184df38314415ae-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-0184df38314415ae-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:38:29.324Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers the approved mock (/tmp/board-shot/mock.png): an ID / Task / Result / Depends on / Checks table, short-ID dependency chips, a dash when there are none, and an '<n> checks' toggle that opens the checks under the row. It also keeps the counts line.","evidence":"I read the mock. It shows the 'PLANNED TASKS' label, the counts line '4 passed, 0 failed, 0 unrecorded, 0 unplanned', and the header 'ID Task Result Depends on Checks'. Its rows read T001..T004 with Passed pills, chips T001/T002/T003 or '—', and toggles '▸ 8 checks' / '▾ 5 checks'. The open row lists the checks under the task. All of these appear in §2.3. [files: /tmp/board-shot/mock.png]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The open checks row lists the checks as a 'plain bulleted list' (§2.3 postcondition).","evidence":"In the mock the open T002 checks row shows plain indented lines with no bullet marks, such as 'stop cancels the provider turn…' and 'stop or detach while a turn waits…'. The design's own Summary says 'opens them as a plain list'. Only the §2.3 postcondition says 'bulleted', so the design contradicts the mock and itself. [files: /tmp/board-shot/mock.png]","action":"State that the checks render as an unbulleted list (ul with list-style:none and no ::before glyph), matching the mock, or confirm that bullets are wanted.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.3","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The ac1–ac3 acceptance criteria named in §5 trace to an upstream spec or triage record.","evidence":"I grepped the repo for '0184df38'. It matches only the LLD itself (docs/standalone/.../S001/LLD.md and .insrc/artifacts/LLD-0184df38314415ae-s1.json). No SPEC or triage artifact defines ac1..ac3, so I could not check the criteria's wording against an upstream source.","action":"Spell out ac1–ac3 in the LLD, or link the triage/spec record that defines them.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today taskRows gives dependsOn as dependency titles through the sourceIds join, keeps the raw PLAN id when no task item joins, and sets dependsOn/acceptanceChecks to null when there is no ok PLAN task.","evidence":"board-details.ts:42 has `itemForPlanId = (planId) => taskItems.find(t => t.sourceIds.includes(planId))`. Lines 55-58 read `dependsOn: planTask === undefined ? null : planTask.dependsOn.map(d => { const dep = itemForPlanId(d); return dep === undefined ? d : titleOf(dep); })`. Line 59 reads `acceptanceChecks: planTask === undefined ? null : [...]`. Lines 45-47 find planTask only when `plan.state === 'ok'`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today taskList renders each task as a <details class='task'> whose summary is only the title (or the taskItemId), with a 'Depends on <titles>' pill and a ballot-box check list. The counts line, the 'No task plan recorded yet.' message and the planNotice follow it.","evidence":"board-host.ts:231-235: `make('details',undefined,'task')`, `make('summary',t.title===null?t.taskItemId:t.title)`, `pill(... 'Depends on '+t.dependsOn.join(', '),'neutral')`, and `make('ul',undefined,'checks')`. Line 228 renders task-counts, line 229 'No task plan recorded yet.', and line 235 plan-notice. CSS at board-host.ts:428 is `.checks li::before{content:\"\\2610  \"...}`, the ballot box. One detail the design leaves out: an empty dependsOn today shows a 'No dependencies' pill, which the design replaces with a dash, as the mock shows. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design reuses existing pieces with their stated shape: the .table-wrap/table.records styling (which scrolls on a narrow column), the pill helper with a tone, and openOf keyed by model.entryId.","evidence":"board-host.ts:237 recordsTable uses `make('div',undefined,'table-wrap')` and `make('table',undefined,'records')`. CSS lines 439-441 style table.records, and lines 452-453 set `.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto;}` and `table.records{min-width:620px;}`. Line 98 defines `pill(text,tone,cls)`. Line 103 declares `const scrollOf={},openOf={};`, and lines 160-162 and 171 key it by `model.entryId+':'+...`. The proposed key `entryId+':checks:'+taskItemId` does not collide with the stage and ':fold' keys. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"shortId and TaskDependencyView are new. No existing helper already derives a task's short id.","evidence":"board-protocol.ts:122-133 TaskRowView has no shortId. compactIdOf in board-model.ts covers card ids only: board-model.test.ts:223 says 'a task id is not a card id and is returned whole'. Adding a separate last-segment rule is therefore justified. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-model.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The rule 'shortId is the last ':'-separated segment' gives T<nnn> for every task item id the daemon mints.","evidence":"src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts:15 and types.ts:83 say task ids take the '<story id>:T<nnn>' form, even under a ':R(<raw>)' story (graph.test.ts:264 has `${EPIC_ID}:R(x):T002`). The last segment is therefore always T<nnn>. [files: src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts, src/workflow/delivery/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The call-site inventory covers every consumer of TaskRowView.dependsOn and of the old task markup: board-protocol.ts, board-details.ts and board-host.ts, plus the tests updated in the migration steps.","evidence":"A grep for dependsOn/TaskRowView in vscode-plugin/src/delivery finds production uses only in board-protocol.ts:129, board-details.ts:55 and board-host.ts:233. details-memory.ts:40 uses PlanTaskView, not TaskRowView. The tests that pin the old shape or markup are board-details.test.ts:48 and :272, board-host.test.ts:442, :456, :558 and :574 (string dependsOn), and board-host.test.ts:1155-1157 and :1172 (details.task). Migration steps 1-2 say to update the view-model and host tests. The §3.1 call-site list could name those test files explicitly. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-details.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-host.test.ts]","action":"Optionally list the pinned test sites (board-details.test.ts:48,272; board-host.test.ts:442,456,558,574,1155-1157,1172) under §3.1 call sites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"TaskRowView is a webview-only shape and is never persisted. Fold memory (openOf) lives only in the webview session.","evidence":"TaskRowView is used only in ItemDetailsViewModel.tasks (board-protocol.ts:174), which is posted to the webview. details-memory.ts stores PLAN tasks (id/dependsOn/acceptanceChecks strings, line 40), not TaskRowView. openOf is a plain in-script object (board-host.ts:103). No migration is needed. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/details-memory.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"When the PLAN cannot be read, the failure is detectable and handled: dependsOn and acceptanceChecks stay null, every task row remains, and planNotice renders under the table.","evidence":"board-details.ts:45-47 finds planTask only when plan.state==='ok', so a failed read yields null dependsOn/acceptanceChecks (lines 55, 59). board-details.ts:213 sets `planNotice: plan.state === 'failed' ? `The plan could not be read: ${plan.message}` : null`. board-host.test.ts:537-538 already checks that the notice shows and the results remain. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-host.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A PLAN dependency with no joining task item is detectable at the existing join and can fall back to { shortId: raw, title: raw }.","evidence":"board-details.ts:56-57: `const dep = itemForPlanId(d); return dep === undefined ? d : titleOf(dep);`. This undefined branch is where the raw-id pair goes. The existing fixture covers the case: board-details.test.ts:44 has `dependsOn: ['t2', 't9']`, and t9 has no task item. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-details.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The integration tests can run the new table and checks toggle (click, aria-expanded, showing and hiding the next row, re-render keeping it open) in the board-webview-harness fake DOM, which forbids innerHTML.","evidence":"board-webview-harness.ts:14 says 'A fake DOM element: records text, attributes, children, listeners and form values; innerHTML throws'. It has generic getAttribute/attrs (line 54) and querySelectorAll (line 56), and listeners are called by the click() helper (board-host.test.ts:1167). Tables already render and are asserted there (board-host.test.ts:1173-1175, the tr rows of records). [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-webview-harness.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-host.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion and edge case has a test.","evidence":"§5 maps ac1 to the board-details taskRows short-id and dependency-pair test, ac2 to the board-host five-column table test, and ac3 to the re-render persistence test. The integration subjects also cover the 'No task plan' case, '1 check' versus '<n> checks', the null-title fallback, and the evidence tab having no task rows. The unit subjects cover the no-':' id and the raw-id dependency. Two edge cases have no named subject: Back between stories keeps separate open choices, and the narrow-column scroll (whose CSS is already asserted by board-host.test.ts:1697 for .table-wrap). Both are low risk. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-host.test.ts]","action":"Optionally add a subject for per-story open choices across open → Back.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":13,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-11T08:38:29.324Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{"coverage-of-intent.2":{"findingId":"coverage-of-intent.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: §2.3 and the test strategy now say the checks render as a plain list with no bullet marks or checkbox glyphs, matching the mock and the summary.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-11T08:40:09.871Z"},"coverage-of-intent.3":{"findingId":"coverage-of-intent.3","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: ac1-ac3 are now spelled out in the acceptance mapping. They are derived from the story spec captured at triage (the user-approved mock /tmp/board-shot/mock.png); the standalone story has no separate SPEC record.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-11T08:40:09.873Z"}}}}}}
